      "side": 1,
      "message": "Calling rdd_interrupt will essentially change the default PHY to the AP phy instead of CCD phy, because rdd_detach is called when the debug cable is not detected. \n\nWith a standard SuzyQ you have to power on the AP for Rd detection to work.\n\nThere are reworked SuzyQs that have Rp/Rp instead of Rd/Rd, which can be detected no matter the state of the AP. There are some issues with that cable because the EC does not currently identify it as a debug accessory, and tries to draw too much power.\n\nOnce we get the reworked SuzyQs and the charging issues with that are fixed, then this wont be a problem.\n\nSo should we change it back to what it was before until the SuzyQ situation is sorted out? or just tell people to hit the power button?",
